From 8b51b0be1d75ab588c0f4a1c36b1468112dbef2d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ClaudeBox <claudebox@local>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 21:18:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fork: M8 two-phase batch block loop behind
 SFU_SEISMIC_M8_BATCH
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Both copies of evaluate_posting_block (posting_list.rs in-RAM +
mmap_index.rs served mmap path) restructured: phase 1 = existing
visited-filter collecting survivors in-order, phase 2 = score in chunks
of 6 via the compute_distances_batch6 evaluator seam, scalar tail <6.
Per-candidate op order preserved exactly (bit-identity by construction);
heap-push order unchanged; scored_in_block semantics unchanged.
Env gate read once per posting-list scan (4 sites), live-flippable
in-process for the paired A/B; =0/false forces the verbatim old loop.
Tests: m8_batch_matches_scalar_exactly (widths 1/2/3/6/13/18, both
loops, mmap<->in-RAM cross-equality) + m8_env_gate_is_live (ragged
multi-term widths, 9 in-process flips).

Also completes the half-committed 2026-07-10 Q3 block_stats signature
changes (posting_list.rs/mmap_index.rs/inverted_index.rs) that had left
HEAD 85e30dd uncompilable — the mmap_io.rs half was committed alone.
